Quick one. Our internal wiki lets several people edit the same page, and last week two folks lost edits. I "fixed" it in this Go change and want a review. Pages have a `version` int column that the loader already returns to the editor.

```go
func (s *PageStore) Save(ctx context.Context, id string, body string) error {
    res, err := s.db.ExecContext(ctx,
        `UPDATE pages SET body = $1, updated_at = now()
         WHERE id = $2 AND deleted_at IS NULL`, body, id)
    if err != nil {
        return err
    }
    n, _ := res.RowsAffected()
    if n == 0 {
        return ErrPageNotFound
    }
    return nil
}
```

The handler passes the editor's body straight to Save. I haven't added a test for Save since it's "just an update".

